This project includes code adapted from:

  FlyGym / NeuroMechFly 2.1.0 (https://github.com/NeLy-EPFL/flygym)
  Copyright 2023-2026 The NeuroMechFly v2 Authors
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (docs/FLYGYM-LICENSE.txt)

  The body construction, reset posture and controller usage in
  backend/src/digitalfly/simulation/engines.py and scripts/smoke_flygym.py
  follow the FlyGym turning-controller tutorial. This project changes the
  ground colors and camera placement and adds a visual target. The fast
  controller path in engines.py re-implements HybridController.step,
  HybridTurningController.step and get_bodysegment_contact_forces with
  precomputed lookups and unchanged arithmetic. The FlyVis column mapping in
  backend/src/digitalfly/vision/flyvis_eyes.py anchors the two eye lattices
  as FlyGym 1.x's RetinaMapper does.

  Drosophila_brain_model (https://github.com/philshiu/Drosophila_brain_model)
  Copyright (c) 2023 Philip Shiu and Nico Spiller
  Licensed under the MIT License (text below)

  The spiking dynamics in backend/src/digitalfly/neural/connectome.py
  re-implement the leaky integrate-and-fire model, constants and Brian2
  update order of Shiu et al. 2024's model.py in NumPy.

  rayshubskiy_elife_102230_secondary_analysis_code
  (https://github.com/wilson-lab/rayshubskiy_elife_102230_secondary_analysis_code)
  Copyright (c) 2025 Wilson Lab
  Licensed under the MIT License (text below)

  detect_spikes, firing_rate and rayshubskiy_recording in
  backend/src/digitalfly/compare.py port the authors' spike detection,
  firing-rate estimation, channel assignment and yaw calibration
  (process_voltage_spike_detection, detect_spikes, bin_spikes, estimate_fr).

